WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:01.492
The monsoon is long gone.

2
00:00:01.492 --> 00:00:02.177
It's January.

3
00:00:02.177 --> 00:00:04.023
So why is it snowing in Kashmir

4
00:00:04.023 --> 00:00:05.705
and raining in Punjab?

5
00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.427
The answer comes from far away.

6
00:00:08.427 --> 00:00:10.807
Storms that form over the Mediterranean region

7
00:00:10.807 --> 00:00:11.782
are carried east,

8
00:00:11.782 --> 00:00:13.199
across West Asia,

9
00:00:13.199 --> 00:00:15.323
by strong westerly winds high in the

10
00:00:15.323 --> 00:00:16.204
sky.

11
00:00:16.604 --> 00:00:19.356
In India we call them western disturbances.

12
00:00:19.356 --> 00:00:20.633
They arrive one after another,

13
00:00:20.633 --> 00:00:22.848
mostly from December to February.

14
00:00:23.248 --> 00:00:25.036
When they meet the Himalayas,

15
00:00:25.036 --> 00:00:27.242
the moist air rises and cools.

16
00:00:27.242 --> 00:00:28.345
The hills get snow,

17
00:00:28.345 --> 00:00:30.017
and the plains below get light winter

18
00:00:30.017 --> 00:00:30.886
rain.

19
00:00:31.285 --> 00:00:33.177
That winter rain matters.

20
00:00:33.177 --> 00:00:34.582
It waters the rabi crops,

21
00:00:34.582 --> 00:00:36.103
especially wheat.

22
00:00:36.103 --> 00:00:37.972
The snow melts in summer and feeds

23
00:00:37.972 --> 00:00:39.062
the rivers.

24
00:00:39.462 --> 00:00:40.948
So the north gets rain from two

25
00:00:40.948 --> 00:00:42.144
directions.

26
00:00:42.144 --> 00:00:44.245
The monsoon from the south-west seas in

27
00:00:44.245 --> 00:00:47.403
summer, and western disturbances from the west

28
00:00:47.403 --> 00:00:48.493
in winter.

29
00:00:48.893 --> 00:00:50.193
For GS One:

30
00:00:50.193 --> 00:00:52.655
Mediterranean origin, carried by the westerlies,

31
00:00:52.655 --> 00:00:54.164
winter rain in the north-west,

32
00:00:54.164 --> 00:00:55.787
good for the rabi crop.

